This folder holds the parts that must exist before Flux can work. Flux does
not manage them. You deploy them by hand.

- base components: ccmd and netd. Deploy them together.
- flux: the Flux controllers.
- gitops: the namespace, the root Kustomization, the notification objects and
  the token template.

The GitRepository is not in this folder. Each release branch holds it in
deploy/release.yaml, so this folder never changes at release time.

On main, the images built in this repo use the latest tag. A release branch
has the real tags.

New cluster? Run in this order:

kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base?ref=release/<tag>
kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base/flux?ref=release/<tag>
kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base/gitops?ref=release/<tag>
kubectl apply -f "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/teapotovh/teapot/release/<tag>/deploy/release.yaml"

The root Kustomization reports a missing source until you apply the release
file. Flux reconciles the rest after that.

Fill in the token in deploy/base/gitops/secret.yaml and apply it by hand after
the steps above. Flux reconciles the rest.

To deploy a release on a running cluster, apply only the release file:

kubectl apply -f "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/teapotovh/teapot/release/<tag>/deploy/release.yaml"
